{# THE PATROL TYPES SECTION OF THE CONFIGURE PAGE — body only.

   NO HEAD, NO STRIP, NO CRUMB, NO WAY BACK. The shell draws all four; this file
   writes the section's content and nothing around it, which is the whole of what
   a rendered section is.

   ONE SECTION, ONE POST. Every base, glyph and tunable below is a field of this
   section, and the design draws ONE save row under them. The add panel's own
   button submits the same form, so a name typed there is created whichever of
   the two buttons is pressed.
   → POST …/configure/types (patrol_types_save)

   A ROW'S RENAME, RETIRE AND REACTIVATE ARE EACH THEIR OWN POST, because each is
   a decision on its own. A form cannot be nested inside another and the shell's
   `.srow > .nm | .cd | .n | .acts` rules are direct-child rules, so each of those
   forms sits at the END of the section and its controls name it with the HTML
   `form` attribute.
   @see https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fae-form

   THE TWO PICKERS ARE RADIOS, NOT BUTTONS. The design draws `<button>`s and a
   script; a section that saves in one POST makes them radios inside their
   labels, so the lit member and the checked one are the same thing and the page
   needs no script to keep them so. The radio itself is `hidden` — clicking the
   label still checks it — and `.sbo:has(input:checked)` is what lights it.

   THE ONE THING THAT DOES NEED A SCRIPT is the tunables disclosure. The design
   hides them behind the row's own Tunables control and its `.stype.shut` class,
   and HTML's own `<details>` cannot do it here: the row is full of buttons and
   inputs, and inside a `<summary>` every one of them would toggle the disclosure
   instead of doing its job. So one Stimulus controller toggles that one class.
   The base picker IS a `<details>`, because its summary is a badge and nothing
   else. #}

{% set save = patrol_url('patrol_types_save', {uuid: area.uuid}) %}

{# Area scope, said once, plainly — the one fact that changes how the section is
   read. #}
<div class="tx-say">{{ ux_icon('patrol:shield', {width: 17, height: 17}) }}<div><b>These patrol types are {{ area.name }}&rsquo;s own.</b>
    Each area keeps its own, so a type added here reaches only the handsets patrolling {{ area.name }}.
    Editing rides on <span class="mono">patrols.manage</span> — the authority over the words everybody else must
    use. Being able to log a patrol (<span class="mono">patrols.record</span>) is not enough.</div></div>

{% if save %}<form method="post" action="{{ save }}">
<input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">{% endif %}
<div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
    <span class="tab">Patrol types<span class="src">· area scope</span></span>
    {# Never deleted: a patrol filed under a type keeps it. Retiring takes it off
       the handset at the next sync and leaves every record intact. The base is a
       fixed key, never a label: the handset resolves what it records from it. #}
    <p class="use">A type carries <b>what it records</b>, and the handset reads it:
        {%- for base in bases %} <b>{{ base.label }}</b> — {{ base.records }}{{ loop.last ? '.' : ';' }}{% endfor %}
        The base is picked when the type is created and can be changed on its row, and it prefills the three numbers
        under it: the pace a patrol of this type is expected to keep, how wide its track counts as covered, and where
        an observation is placed.</p>

    {% for type in types %}
        {% set n = typeCounts[type.key]|default(0) %}
        {% set defaults = type.base ? baseDefaults[type.base.value] : null %}
        <div class="stype shut" {{ stimulus_controller('@uhifadhi/patrol-module/disclose') }}>
            <div class="srow{{ type.active ? '' : ' gone' }}">
                <span class="nm">{{ type.label }}</span>
                <span class="cd">{{ type.key }}</span>
                {% if not type.active %}<span class="chip idle">retired</span>{% endif %}
                {% if save %}
                    {# CLOSED, THE BADGE; OPEN, THE TWO PICKERS. `.ask` is a type
                       nobody has answered for yet — a control, because the row is
                       asking, and never an error. #}
                    <details>
                        <summary class="sbase{{ type.base ? '' : ' ask' }}">
                            {{- ux_icon('patrol:' ~ typeGlyphs[type.uuid], {width: 13, height: 13}) -}}
                            {{ type.base ? type.base.label : 'choose base' }}
                        </summary>
                        <span class="sbpick row" role="group" aria-label="What {{ type.label }} records">
                            {% for base in bases %}
                                <label class="sbo">
                                    <input type="radio" name="base[{{ type.uuid }}]" value="{{ base.value }}"
                                           {{ type.base == base ? 'checked' : '' }} hidden>
                                    {{- ux_icon('patrol:' ~ baseDefaults[base.value].glyph, {width: 13, height: 13}) -}}
                                    {{ base.label }}
                                </label>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </span>
                        <span class="sbicon" role="group" aria-label="The glyph {{ type.label }} wears">
                            {% for glyph in glyphs %}
                                <label class="sbi" title="{{ glyph }}">
                                    <input type="radio" name="glyph[{{ type.uuid }}]" value="{{ glyph }}"
                                           {{ type.glyph == glyph ? 'checked' : '' }} hidden>
                                    {{- ux_icon('patrol:' ~ glyph, {width: 13, height: 13}) -}}
                                </label>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </span>
                    </details>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="sbase{{ type.base ? '' : ' ask' }}">
                        {{- ux_icon('patrol:' ~ typeGlyphs[type.uuid], {width: 13, height: 13}) -}}
                        {{ type.base ? type.base.label : 'no base' }}
                    </span>
                {% endif %}
                <span class="n">{{ n }} {{ n == 1 ? 'patrol' : 'patrols' }}</span>
                <span class="acts">
                    <button class="sact" type="button"
                            {{ stimulus_action('@uhifadhi/patrol-module/disclose', 'toggle') }}>Tunables<i class="cv"></i></button>
                    {% if save %}
                        {# THE FIELD IS DISCLOSED BY THE ROW'S OWN RENAME CONTROL. A
                           field open on every row turns a list of words into a page
                           of form controls.
                           @see https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#the-details-element #}
                        <details>
                            <summary class="sact">Rename</summary>
                            <input class="fld" style="width:150px" type="text" name="label" value="{{ type.label }}"
                                   form="patrol-type-rename-{{ type.uuid }}" aria-label="Rename {{ type.label }}" required>
                            <button class="sact" type="submit" form="patrol-type-rename-{{ type.uuid }}">Save</button>
                        </details>
                        {% if type.active %}
                            <button class="sact warn" type="submit" form="patrol-type-retire-{{ type.uuid }}">Retire</button>
                        {% else %}
                            <button class="sact" type="submit" form="patrol-type-reactivate-{{ type.uuid }}">Reactivate</button>
                        {% endif %}
                    {% endif %}
                </span>
            </div>
            <div class="stun">
                <div class="tn">
                    <span class="lb">pace</span>
                    <input class="fld" type="number" name="pace_min[{{ type.uuid }}]" min="{{ minPaceKmh }}" max="{{ maxPaceKmh }}"
                           value="{{ type.paceMinKmh }}" aria-label="Slowest pace for {{ type.label }}"{{ save ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
                    <span class="to">&ndash;</span>
                    <input class="fld" type="number" name="pace_max[{{ type.uuid }}]" min="{{ minPaceKmh }}" max="{{ maxPaceKmh }}"
                           value="{{ type.paceMaxKmh }}" aria-label="Fastest pace for {{ type.label }}"{{ save ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
                    <span class="u">km/h</span>
                </div>
                <div class="tn">
                    <span class="lb">coverage buffer</span>
                    <input class="fld" type="number" name="buffer[{{ type.uuid }}]" min="{{ minBufferM }}" max="{{ maxBufferM }}"
                           value="{{ type.coverageBufferM }}" aria-label="Coverage buffer for {{ type.label }}"{{ save ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
                    <span class="u">m</span>
                </div>
                <div class="tn">
                    <span class="lb">observations</span>
                    <span class="sbpick" role="group" aria-label="Where an observation of {{ type.label }} is placed">
                        {% for placement in placements %}
                            <label class="sbo">
                                <input type="radio" name="placement[{{ type.uuid }}]" value="{{ placement.value }}"
                                       {{ type.observationPlacement == placement ? 'checked' : '' }}{{ save ? '' : ' disabled' }} hidden>
                                {{ placement.label }}
                            </label>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </span>
                </div>
                {% if defaults %}
                    <span class="from">Prefilled from the <b>{{ type.base.label }}</b> base:
                        {{ defaults.sentence }}. A number changed here belongs to this type alone.</span>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="from">Nothing is prefilled until this type is given a base. A number typed here
                        belongs to this type alone.</span>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="srow"><span class="nm">No patrol types are configured.</span></div>
    {% endfor %}

    {% if save %}
        <div class="saddcard">
            <span class="hd">Add a patrol type</span>
            <div class="saddrow">
                <input class="fld" type="text" name="label" placeholder="Name of the new patrol type"
                       aria-label="New patrol type">
                <span class="lb">records</span>
                <span class="sbpick" role="group" aria-label="What the new type records">
                    {% for base in bases %}
                        <label class="sbo">
                            <input type="radio" name="add_base" value="{{ base.value }}" hidden>
                            {{- ux_icon('patrol:' ~ baseDefaults[base.value].glyph, {width: 14, height: 14}) -}}
                            {{ base.label }}
                        </label>
                    {% endfor %}
                </span>
                <span class="lb">glyph</span>
                <span class="sbicon" role="group" aria-label="The glyph the new type wears">
                    {% for glyph in glyphs %}
                        <label class="sbi" title="{{ glyph }}">
                            <input type="radio" name="add_glyph" value="{{ glyph }}" hidden>
                            {{- ux_icon('patrol:' ~ glyph, {width: 14, height: 14}) -}}
                        </label>
                    {% endfor %}
                </span>
                <button class="sadd" type="submit">+ Add type</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>

{% if save %}
    {# NO CANCEL LINK OUT OF THE MODULE. The section strip, the lit Configure and
       the crumb are the ways back; a fourth would be the thing the frame
       replaced. #}
    <div class="save-row"><button class="cta" type="submit">Save patrol types</button></div>
</form>

    {# The row forms, at the end of the section, named by the controls above. #}
    {% for type in types %}
        {% for action in ['rename', 'retire', 'reactivate'] %}
            <form id="patrol-type-{{ action }}-{{ type.uuid }}" method="post"
                  action="{{ patrol_url('patrol_type_act', {uuid: area.uuid, type: type.uuid, action: action}) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            </form>
        {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
{% endif %}
